    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Set the draft cover from an image URL, local image, or timeline frame\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --minidraft TEXT    Minidraft JSON content for cover patch mode (bypass engine)\r\n          --image TEXT Excludes: --frame --url \r\n                              Set cover from a local image path\r\n          --url TEXT Excludes: --image --frame \r\n                              Set cover from a remote image URL\r\n          --frame <duration>  Set cover from a draft timeline frame; explicit unit required\r\n                              (us, ms, s, min)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --image /tmp/cover.jpg\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --url https://example.com/cover.jpg\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --frame 3.5s\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --url https://example.com/cover.jpg --minidraft '{...}'\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Set the draft cover from an image URL, local image, or timeline frame\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --minidraft TEXT    Minidraft JSON content for cover patch mode (bypass engine)\r\n          --image TEXT Excludes: --frame --url \r\n                              Set cover from a local image path\r\n          --url TEXT Excludes: --image --frame \r\n                              Set cover from a remote image URL\r\n          --frame <duration>  Set cover from a draft timeline frame; explicit unit required\r\n                              (us, ms, s, min)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --image /tmp/cover.jpg\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --url https://example.com/cover.jpg\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --ref local://demo --frame 3.5s\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft cover set --url https://example.com/cover.jpg --minidraft '{...}'\r\n",
